    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15138" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀριστο-τόκος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bearing the best children,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γαστήρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>C.</u>
					3.62
				</span></i>
			:—poet. fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀριστοτόκεια</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰρ]</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				24.73
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Tryph.
				401
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(5).292
			</span></i>(<span class="entity">Paros</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀριστότοκος, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,</span>
			<i>born of the best parents,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γέννα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					909
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
				896
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Syria</span>).</div>
